---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro"
import { DEPLOY } from "@scudra/shared"
---

<Layout
  title="The Analyst — Scudra"
  description="Blast Radius Zero. An LLM writes code that runs in a locked-down, throwaway container. Built for the Vultr Agent Rush hackathon."
>
  <article class="sc-container py-20 max-w-[72ch]" data-reveal>
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-muted mb-4">
      <a href="/experiences" class="no-underline text-inherit hover:text-ink">← Experiences</a>
    </p>

    <h1 class="font-serif text-[clamp(2.25rem,5vw,3.5rem)] leading-[1.1] tracking-tight mb-4">
      The Analyst
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-8">
      Blast Radius Zero. An LLM writes code that runs in a locked-down, throwaway container on a cloud VM. Real output, self-repair, a one-click "attack the sandbox" containment demo, and verified teardown.
    </p>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mb-12">
      <a
        href={DEPLOY.analyst.url}
        class="sc-button-primary"
      >
        Try the live demo
      </a>
      <a
        href="https://youtu.be/8iDC_EZxAu4"
        class="sc-button-secondary"
      >
        Watch the demo
      </a>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/sneldao/scudra/tree/main/apps/analyst"
        class="sc-button-secondary"
      >
        View source
      </a>
      <a
        href="/recipes/code-interpreter"
        class="sc-button-secondary"
      >
        Read the recipe
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="p-6 bg-paper-warm rounded-sc border border-black/5">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl mb-4">What it demonstrates</h2>
      <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 text-ink-muted leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
        <li><strong>Provider-agnostic sandbox.</strong> A small provider interface with a hardened Docker implementation — no network, no secrets, capped resources, verified teardown.</li>
        <li><strong>Bounded self-repair.</strong> The agent loop retries failed code a limited number of times, then gives up cleanly.</li>
        <li><strong>Blast Radius Zero.</strong> A seven-probe containment board lets you attack the sandbox and watch every escape attempt fail.</li>
        <li><strong>Verified answers.</strong> A second model judges whether the output actually answers the task — and the verdict is signed into the receipt.</li>
        <li><strong>Signed receipts.</strong> Every run produces an Ed25519-signed receipt — the public key is published, so anyone can verify it, or try to forge it.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
